Welcome! This is the blog attached to my academic site. I'll use it for research
notes, short write-ups on explainable AI and process mining, and the occasional
walkthrough of a method or paper.

## What to expect

- **Research notes** — half-formed ideas, reading summaries, and things I want to
  remember.
- **Method walkthroughs** — occasionally with interactive, scroll-driven visuals
  (the site ships a scrollytelling template built for exactly that).
- **Meta posts** like this one.

## How this is built

The site is a static [Astro](https://astro.build) project. Posts are just Markdown
(or MDX) files in `src/content/blog/` with a little frontmatter:

```yaml
---
title: "My post"
description: "One-line summary."
pubDate: 2026-07-12
tags: ["xai"]
---
```

Add a file, and it shows up here automatically. That's the whole workflow.

## Switch to MDX…

We can Switch to MDX and drop components straight into the prose — callouts like the one in the mdx example, and,
if a post calls for it, the site's scrollytelling components for a scroll-driven
walkthrough.

<Callout type="tip">
  Write everyday posts in plain <code>.md</code>. Reach for <code>.mdx</code> only
  when a post needs interactive pieces.
</Callout>
